From ec64826328fce6da6913d9274158632f67a812cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 16:11:46 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(test): isolate CLI subprocess tests from the shared repo
 checkout

The CLI registry suite spawned bin/forge.js with the repo checkout as cwd,
so every spawn resolved projectRoot to the real working tree and read/wrote
its .forge state. scripts/test-full-suite.js runs shards concurrently, so
those spawns raced each other and returned fast, wrong answers.

Each spawn now gets a private git-init'd sandbox as both cwd and INIT_CWD,
with FORGE_*/INIT_CWD scrubbed from the inherited env. Inner spawn timeout
goes 10s -> 30s (spawns were measured at 10.1-10.6s under shard load, so 10s
bounded noise, not a hang) and a timeout now throws instead of masquerading
as exit 1.

Kernel issue 15587fd6

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
